# Rust build products
/target
# Not committed, matching every other Day app repo: the day dependency floats on `main`, and a
# lock resolved against a local checkout (`day patch`) records paths meaningless on any other
# machine.
Cargo.lock

# day build outputs: per-target cargo dirs, staged assets, jniLibs, screenshots, dist artifacts,
# and the gradle/xcodebuild/hvigor outputs under the platform scaffolds
build/

# Machine-local: `day patch --local <day-checkout>` writes this to build against a checkout
# instead of the git dependency. CI has no such file and resolves git.
/.cargo/config.toml

# Gradle local state (the android scaffold is source; its caches are not)
.gradle/
local.properties

# SwiftPM build products of the app's own Swift package (docs/swiftui.md); `day build` compiles
# it via the generated DayPieces package, `swift test` uses this local scratch.
swiftui/.build/

# Xcode local state (DayApp.xcodeproj itself is hand-written source — do NOT ignore it)
xcuserdata/
DerivedData/
# Xcode writes SwiftPM bookkeeping INSIDE the .xcodeproj the first time it resolves packages.
# It is regenerated state, and project.xcworkspace cannot be relocated out of the project.
**/*.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/

# Logs
*.log

.DS_Store

# The website is generated from repo data; only site.toml and theme.css are source.
website/.daysite/
website/appindex.json
website/gallery-manifest.json
